THOUGHT: `getFilter()` is abstract and may return null, so NullAway flags dereferencing `filter` in `configure`. Other methods either assert non-null or pass it to APIs that likely require non-null. To fix only this error safely, I can add a local null check in `configure` before using `filter.getClass()`, falling back to the default dispatcher types when `filter` is null. Then I must run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/spring-boot && sed -i '225,232s/T filter = getFilter();/T filter = getFilter();
				if (filter == null) {
					dispatcherTypes = EnumSet.of(DispatcherType.REQUEST);
				}
				else if (ClassUtils.isPresent("org.springframework.web.filter.OncePerRequestFilter",
						filter.getClass().getClassLoader()) && filter instanceof OncePerRequestFilter) {
					dispatcherTypes = EnumSet.allOf(DispatcherType.class);
				}
				else {
					dispatcherTypes = EnumSet.of(DispatcherType.REQUEST);
				}/' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/web/servlet/AbstractFilterRegistrationBean.java && ./gradlew :spring-boot-project:spring-boot:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "DEREFERENCE_NULLABLE" -n new_build_output.log || true```

